  <!-- Results. -->
  <section class="hero is-small">
    <!-- <section class="section"> -->
    <div class="hero-body ">
      <hr>
      <div class="container " id="reproducing_results">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <h2 style="
            font-size: 2rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ff7eb3, #ff758c, #ff6a00);
            -webkit-background-clip: text;
            -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
            display: inline-block;
            position: relative;
          ">
            Reproduce Our Results
          </h2>
          <div style="
            height: 3px;
            width: 80px;
            margin: 0.5rem auto 0;
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ff7eb3, #ff758c, #ff6a00);
            border-radius: 2px;
          "></div>
        </div>
        <div class="content has-text-justified" style="font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8;">
        <p>Our work builds directly on Self Forcing and can be readily reproduced by following the algorithm below.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="image is-centered">
          <img src="images/algorithm.png">
        </figure>
        <div class="content has-text-justified" style="font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <p>
            In short, it can be implemented on top of Self Forcing by making the following 3 changes:
            <ol>
              <li>Self roll out videos beyond the teacher's horizon with rolling KV Cache.</li>
              <li>Uniformly sample continuous latent frames from the long video and apply DMD with backward noise initialization. </li>
              <li>[Optional] Post train the model with GRPO with your preferred rewards.</li>
            </ol>
          </p>
          Our method uses exactly the same inference code as Self Forcing.
        </div>

      </div>








   

